From 78ffb87e94785e0bb907afc26b5ab11dde3c2778 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shreyan <shreyanshukla19@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 15:21:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] record: lerobot-record-cmd, a command channel next to the
 keys (copy, record loop unchanged)

A separate entry point for pages and scripts: lerobot-record-cmd takes the same arguments as
lerobot-record and runs the unchanged lerobot_record.record(). It binds a local ZMQ REP socket
(tcp://127.0.0.1:5730, LEROBOT_RECORD_CMD to change or "off") before anything connects, and
wraps two module globals only:
- init_keyboard_listener: the channel writes into the same events dict as the keys
  (next = right arrow, discard = left arrow, return = 'a', stop = esc), same flags, same
  console lines; the keyboard keeps working as the fallback.
- record_loop: publishes the phase (recording / waiting), the episode index and the saved count
  for {"cmd": "state"}.

Ctrl-C is not touched: it still reaches record() and releases torque immediately. The channel's
stop is the ordinary end of collection (esc), never an emergency stop.

Tests: every command sets exactly its key's flags; socket round trip, busy port, SIGINT handler
unchanged; the real record() with the mock robot driven only through the channel (2 episodes
saved, state reports waiting/saved). tests/test_record_manual_advance.py unchanged and passing.

Requested by Kento (2026-11-01 Slack, request 4): separate copy, keys as fallback, e-stop
independent of the channel, branch for review, not merged by us.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
